      "analysis_required": "Native89 confirms the complete ten-piece final checked board after Ra7+: White Kc5/Ra7/b6/c4/f2/h3 against Kb7/Rf7/g7/g5, Black to move. Kc8 and Kb8 are the only legal replies. Independent Kc8/b7+/Kd8 demonstrates that b7+ does not force Kb8. Independent Kb8/Ra8+/Kxa8/b7+/Kb8 is legal but leaves a nine-piece position with the pawn blocked on b7 by Black Kb8: b8=Q is illegal while b8 is occupied. This is a comparison, not a recommended line or a recovered source score. Preserve both rooks until actual capture and all six pawns. The winner badge is not an exact conversion certificate. Verify every rook/king defense, pawn race and complete larger ending; previous eleven- and ten-piece drafts and review history remain preserved. Full board images/captions are available."
